    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d480">

                <pb facs="0465" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg367"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Nabeshima.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-27"><hi rendition="#italic">June 27,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Nabeshima</hi>: In regard to the suggestion
                    of the dispatch of Japanese reenforcements in China, I have pleasure in saying
                    that this Government, speaking for itself, sees no objection to such a
                    proceeding, though the President thinks it advisable that the assent of the
                    other powers be obtained.</p>
                <p>I am, very sincerely, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
